  "review_conclusions": [
    "The operation identity combines origin,nonzero sequence and nonce. One allocator issues each sequence at most once,starting at1;MAX is issued once then zero remains an exhaustion sentinel. Relaxed CAS allocates identities without publishing other state.",
    "Hub,CLI and Application keep process-level OnceLock allocators. Validated operation fields pass into launch requests and session records; the request and DTO alone do not confer admission or an OS lease.",
    "All custom Deserialize paths reuse the same constructors/parsers: nil origin/nonce,zero sequence,invalid subasset and invalid relative paths cannot bypass their value constraints. Serde derives/macros are distinguished from runtime registration and FFI; no such entry exists in the39 formal files.",
    "AssetRef stores GUID,path hint and optional subasset label. Construction validates label shape; the Runtime caller separately checks GUID/path registry agreement and one physical source before serializing. The builtin persisted variant validates its locator scheme,while retired references defer identity resolution to the supplied resolver.",
    "Project names enforce portable single-component text rules. RelPath normalizes separators/removes empty segments and rejects traversal,device and prefix/stream forms. These lexical checks do not establish physical containment; filesystem authorities and asset-root registration are separate caller obligations.",
    "CanonicalDescriptorIdentity validates path shape only. ProjectGuid rejects nil but does not prove uniqueness;manifest digest hashes exact supplied bytes and canonicalizes its wire hex. ProjectIdentity combines three owned values without reading files or checking correspondence. Preflight revalidation and later admission remain caller work.",
    "The9 owned test files cover31 concrete test functions,including allocator exhaustion,wire rejection,reference historical bytes,portable names/paths,digest/identity and project/builtin variants. They were read and statically inspected; none was executed."
  ],
